# Scenario guest-assert-mismatch (plan 04-20, D-20): outcome guest-fail, exit 10. The original
# diagnostic with one wrong expected word: the loop sum 1..10 at 0204 is 0037, this assert says
# 0036, so the one failing clause is named in the detail.
# expect-detail: assert=13 line=24 mem 0204 == 0036 got 0037
ivss 1
id guest-assert-mismatch
profile intv-2609-ntsc-family-p1
content exec boot-stub
content grom zero-grom
content cart diag-cpu-1.ivsc
run-to 4000 cpu-cycles stop halted
assert halted == yes
assert reg R0 == 03C5
assert reg R1 == 8080
assert reg R2 == 0000
assert reg R3 == 0037
assert reg R4 == 0201
assert reg R5 == 0037
assert reg R6 == 0340
assert mem 0200 == 7FFF
assert mem 0201 == 8080
assert mem 0202 == A0A0
assert mem 0203 == 7070
assert mem 0204 == 0036
assert mem 0205 == 0037
assert mem 0206 == 0340
assert mem 0207 == 0201
assert mem 0208 == 7FFF
assert mem 020F == 03C5
